{"title":"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/0/760908564be5459d977ffc2dc18bdd5e55278750.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> is plotted on the graph shown.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/0/760908564be5459d977ffc2dc18bdd5e55278750.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> is reflected in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis, the resulting point is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/9/979c0e5af0a3b0cf6cbcc5793eeb697fa6a1fdfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ (5, -7) \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ (-5, -7) \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ (5, 7) \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ (7, 5) \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ (-7, -5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"578\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When a point is reflected across the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> coordinate doesn't change but the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> coordinate is multiplied by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />. Applying this to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/0/760908564be5459d977ffc2dc18bdd5e55278750.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, we see that the reflected point is located at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/a/69a339c392b76f12b7864af18218e7eb61fb485f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } (5, -7)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"103\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEM